1
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:37,537
You can't change the past,

2
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:39,956
but you can still allow yourself
to be happy again,

3
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,875
especially once you've found it.

4
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:44,544
I think I've found
the perfect bouquet for my wedding.

5
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:47,297
You're the perfect maid of honor, Alex.

6
00:00:53,511 --> 00:00:54,804
You're not funny.

7
00:01:09,527 --> 00:01:12,822
What information is it
that no one else should know?

8
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:16,659
Just a reminder.
Whatever it is you're planning to do,

9
00:01:17,243 --> 00:01:19,412
I can still send both of you back to jail.

10
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:26,711
it's more of a personal matter.

11
00:01:28,087 --> 00:01:30,173
A personal matter?

12
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:37,388
Here, let me have that.

13
00:01:49,734 --> 00:01:53,196
Can you tell me what
really happened last night?

14
00:01:53,822 --> 00:01:57,158
It all started when we met
back in high school.

15
00:01:57,742 --> 00:02:00,328
I even considered her
my childhood sweetheart.

16
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:10,213
I wasn't asking about your love life.

17
00:02:10,296 --> 00:02:13,716
I want to know what you saw
during that fight at the corner.

18
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,677
Oh, that?

19
00:02:18,179 --> 00:02:19,639
We were also waiting for that.

20
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:22,058
Here's what happened.

21
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:28,648
<i>I was drinking with my buddies.</i>

22
00:02:29,149 --> 00:02:32,360
<i>Then I excused myself to take a leak.</i>

23
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:36,656
<i>But when I came back out,</i>
<i>they were all lying on the ground.</i>

24
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:44,831
Did the person have tattoos,
a mustache, a beard?

25
00:02:44,914 --> 00:02:47,333
Tall? Long hair? A mustache?

26
00:02:47,417 --> 00:02:48,585
Male? Female?

27
00:02:48,668 --> 00:02:51,588
Or maybe part of the LGBTQIA++ community?

28
00:02:51,671 --> 00:02:54,424
Tall, short, skinny, heavyset,
what was it?

29
00:02:54,507 --> 00:02:56,175
Like that?

30
00:02:56,259 --> 00:02:58,678
Honestly, I didn't get a good look.

31
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:01,556
But what I did notice…

32
00:03:02,473 --> 00:03:04,392
It was flying.

33
00:03:05,435 --> 00:03:07,270
What was it? A manananggal?

34
00:03:07,937 --> 00:03:10,732
If it was a manananggal,
why was its body still intact?

35
00:03:11,316 --> 00:03:12,609
It wasn't a manananggal.

36
00:03:13,776 --> 00:03:16,195
Mario, that's your opinion, but…

37
00:03:19,365 --> 00:03:20,533
Sorry, Attorney.

38
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:23,536
So, anything else to add?

39
00:03:24,454 --> 00:03:26,789
I'm sorry, but I was
pretty drunk that night,

40
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:29,751
so I don't really know

41
00:03:29,834 --> 00:03:31,544
what exactly I saw.

42
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:33,171
You sure talk a lot,

43
00:03:39,093 --> 00:03:42,055
What a shame, you drunk.

44
00:03:42,138 --> 00:03:45,975
You're no help at all. We should've
just watched the CCTV footage.

45
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:48,937
There's CCTV?

46
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,689
Didn't I mention that?

47
00:04:01,157 --> 00:04:03,785
Captain Pepe, isn't that Jan-Jan?

48
00:04:04,494 --> 00:04:06,663
Yes, I think that's you.

49
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:08,414
That's the two of you.

50
00:04:08,498 --> 00:04:09,624
There!

51
00:04:09,707 --> 00:04:11,167
One bald guy.

52
00:04:12,085 --> 00:04:12,961
One short guy.

53
00:04:13,044 --> 00:04:15,797
No, not that one. This one.

54
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:18,007
There.

55
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,139
Good grief.

56
00:04:26,015 --> 00:04:27,475
Can't that get any clearer?

57
00:04:28,434 --> 00:04:31,771
The captain didn't have the budget
for an HD CCTV camera.

58
00:04:39,153 --> 00:04:40,863
What do you think, Mario?

59
00:04:41,656 --> 00:04:42,907
What do I think?

60
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:48,621
I have a bad feeling about this.

61
00:04:58,464 --> 00:05:00,383
Well, well, well!

62
00:05:00,466 --> 00:05:01,676
Looking good!

63
00:05:01,759 --> 00:05:03,803
- How is it?
- It fits you perfectly!

64
00:05:03,886 --> 00:05:05,305
It fits you perfectly, Mikoy.

65
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:06,347
Isn’t it cool?

66
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:09,976
- So handsome!
- Miks, turn around a little.

67
00:05:10,059 --> 00:05:12,020
- Give us a spin.
- This feels cool!

68
00:05:12,603 --> 00:05:13,855
- It's cool.
- Whoa!

69
00:05:13,938 --> 00:05:15,356
Oh, no!

70
00:05:15,857 --> 00:05:17,066
Miss Taylor.

71
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:17,984
Why is there a tear in the back?

72
00:05:18,067 --> 00:05:18,901
- What's that?
- Why was it cut?

73
00:05:18,985 --> 00:05:22,030
I don't know either, but just relax, okay?

74
00:05:22,113 --> 00:05:24,907
It's just a fitting. Just a fitting.

75
00:05:27,285 --> 00:05:29,871
Everything can be fixed
with proper measurements.

76
00:05:29,954 --> 00:05:31,456
Didn't I tell you?

77
00:05:31,539 --> 00:05:35,084
The secret is all in the measurements.

78
00:05:35,168 --> 00:05:36,002
Right?

79
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:38,880
Buddy Mikoy,

80
00:05:39,422 --> 00:05:40,965
I'm not the crying type,

81
00:05:41,049 --> 00:05:44,177
but I can already picture
your happy ending with Chiara.

82
00:05:45,636 --> 00:05:47,346
It's touching.

83
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:49,140
- Here we go.
- Hey, Captain Pepe, don't be like that.

84
00:05:49,223 --> 00:05:50,641
Captain Pepe, Captain Pepe.

85
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:52,560
- I'm getting goosebumps.
- So, there you go, see?

86
00:05:53,352 --> 00:05:54,562
- Oh, dear.
- Of course.

87
00:05:54,645 --> 00:05:56,773
That's our Captain Pepe.

88
00:05:56,856 --> 00:05:57,982
Come on, Captain Pepe!

89
00:06:00,318 --> 00:06:01,778
We're just having the fitting.

90
00:06:01,861 --> 00:06:03,362
It's just so heartwarming.

91
00:06:03,446 --> 00:06:05,073
But don't worry.

92
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:07,700
On my wedding day,
I'll be waiting for your tears of joy.

93
00:06:07,784 --> 00:06:09,869
There you go!

94
00:06:09,952 --> 00:06:11,996
Come on, you're only tearing up

95
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:14,415
because it reminds you
of your canceled wedding.

96
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:16,375
Whoa!

97
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:18,294
You have a TOTGA, Captain Pepe?

98
00:06:18,377 --> 00:06:19,587
- You have a TOTGA?
- I do.

99
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:21,798
- You do? I never knew that!
- Who?

100
00:06:21,881 --> 00:06:22,715
Tell us the story!

101
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:26,094
- Wait, let me summarize his TOTGA.
- Go ahead, go ahead.

102
00:06:26,177 --> 00:06:27,011
Go ahead.

103
00:06:27,095 --> 00:06:28,179
TOTGA.

104
00:06:28,262 --> 00:06:30,181
Tried. Yes.

105
00:06:30,264 --> 00:06:32,683
Turned down. Goodbye. Ouch!

106
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:33,601
Ouch!

107
00:06:33,684 --> 00:06:35,436
- Ouch!
- Oh, gosh.

108
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:37,772
You sure know a lot.
That's all in the past!

109
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:41,025
- Let's focus on the present.
- Right.

110
00:06:41,109 --> 00:06:43,569
Mikoy and Chiara.

111
00:06:43,653 --> 00:06:45,530
That's what we should look forward to.
So exciting!

112
00:06:45,613 --> 00:06:46,531
That's right!

113
00:06:47,281 --> 00:06:49,283
I can't wait to see it!

114
00:06:49,867 --> 00:06:51,577
- See what?
- I'm so excited.

115
00:06:51,661 --> 00:06:52,954
There's the tear.

116
00:06:58,459 --> 00:06:59,544
Oh my God!

117
00:06:59,627 --> 00:07:01,629
Hold on.

118
00:07:01,712 --> 00:07:05,633
It's not even your wedding yet,
but I'm already tearing up for you.

119
00:07:05,716 --> 00:07:07,844
You look gorgeous!

120
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:10,471
You're so dramatic.

121
00:07:10,555 --> 00:07:14,058
Call me dramatic if you want,
but my feelings are valid.

122
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:15,143
Look at that!

123
00:07:15,643 --> 00:07:17,145
You look beautiful!

124
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:20,022
But it's true, Chiara. You look radiant.

125
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:22,775
You're glowing. You look amazing!
It suits you perfectly.

126
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:34,662
Take your time.

127
00:07:38,958 --> 00:07:41,836
It has to fit you perfectly,

128
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:45,339
and you're the only one
who can decide that.

129
00:07:45,423 --> 00:07:48,593
Not me, and certainly not them.

130
00:07:48,676 --> 00:07:53,598
And when you can picture yourself
wearing that gown on your wedding day,

131
00:07:54,182 --> 00:07:56,517
that's your sign.

132
00:07:56,601 --> 00:08:00,021
The sign that you've found
the right dress.

133
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:08,112
Can I try on a few more?

134
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:13,576
Girls, please take note
of all the adjustments.

135
00:08:13,659 --> 00:08:14,911
Wow.

136
00:08:14,994 --> 00:08:16,245
- Perfect.
- Oh, come on.

137
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:19,624
Come with us.

138
00:08:19,707 --> 00:08:22,460
- Wait, wait. What is going on here?
- Chief, easy!

139
00:08:22,543 --> 00:08:24,212
Where are you taking Mr. Viktor?

140
00:08:25,463 --> 00:08:27,507
- Just relax.
- Stay out of this.

141
00:08:41,145 --> 00:08:41,979
Sit down!

142
00:08:43,064 --> 00:08:44,357
Do not fight.

143
00:09:05,211 --> 00:09:06,212
Sofie.

144
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:12,593
You know what? Enough with that.

145
00:09:12,677 --> 00:09:15,137
We both know our mornings
don't get any better

146
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:16,764
when we see each other.

147
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:22,728
Looks like you're going through something,
and you're taking it out on me.

148
00:09:26,774 --> 00:09:29,610
please excuse me. I'm feeling sleepy.

149
00:09:32,613 --> 00:09:34,574
You know what? You're fake.

150
00:09:37,868 --> 00:09:39,704
What are you talking about?

151
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:43,958
First, you came up to me
and introduced yourself.

152
00:09:44,041 --> 00:09:47,420
Then you warned me
that Angelito was a red flag,

153
00:09:47,503 --> 00:09:49,880
when in fact, he's the complete opposite.

154
00:09:49,964 --> 00:09:50,965
Why?

155
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:52,842
Because you like him.

156
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:55,011
Second,

157
00:09:55,094 --> 00:09:59,390
you pretended to be my friend,
even though you knew I liked Angelito.

158
00:09:59,473 --> 00:10:01,601
And yet here you are,

159
00:10:02,184 --> 00:10:05,688
trying to insert yourself
into a two-person story.

160
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:10,234
You're a mistress, a homewrecker,
and a boyfriend stealer!

161
00:10:11,193 --> 00:10:13,571
You keep calling me a mistress
and a homewrecker,

162
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:17,742
as if you and Angelito
are actually together. So? Are you?

163
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:23,623
Or are you just suffering
from main character syndrome?

164
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:26,917
You should check
your relationship status first

165
00:10:28,127 --> 00:10:30,963
before making a scene like this.

166
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:32,173
And make sure

167
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:37,428
you actually have the right to do so,
so you don't end up looking desperate.

168
00:10:43,059 --> 00:10:46,228
Between the two of us,
you're the desperate one

169
00:10:46,312 --> 00:10:50,441
for clinging to Angelito
like a leech desperate for love.

170
00:10:52,568 --> 00:10:53,694
You know what?

171
00:10:53,778 --> 00:10:55,196
Say goodbye to your hair,

172
00:10:55,279 --> 00:10:57,490
because you're definitely going
to miss it, witch!

173
00:11:00,826 --> 00:11:02,453
He liked me first!

174
00:11:02,536 --> 00:11:05,456
No, you let go. Let Angelito decide.

175
00:11:12,546 --> 00:11:14,173
Look what you did!

176
00:11:14,256 --> 00:11:16,092
You started it!

177
00:11:16,175 --> 00:11:17,760
Because you're such a flirt!

178
00:11:17,843 --> 00:11:19,011
You're the bigger flirt!

179
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:25,309
Bok!

180
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:28,437
You know what?

181
00:11:30,272 --> 00:11:32,358
I have good news for you.

182
00:11:32,441 --> 00:11:35,319
Make sure it's only good news
and doesn't come with bad news.

183
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:37,696
- What is it?
- It's good news.

184
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:43,411
<i>We were getting annoyed because</i>
<i>he kept hanging around the office.</i>

185
00:11:45,162 --> 00:11:47,706
Looks like he finally got tired
and stopped coming here.

186
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:50,334
Even his public appearances
have become rare.

187
00:11:51,627 --> 00:11:53,129
That does sound like good news.

188
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:57,174
Maybe he finally realized
his request was pointless.

189
00:11:58,092 --> 00:12:00,094
And thankfully, I won't have
to bring it up

190
00:12:00,177 --> 00:12:01,846
with Chiara and Mikoy anymore.

191
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:05,766
See? I told you it was good news.

192
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:14,692
Delicious!

193
00:12:15,943 --> 00:12:19,321
Did you taste the nutty caramel notes,

194
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:26,745
No.

195
00:12:29,498 --> 00:12:31,459
I don't really know much about coffee.

196
00:12:31,542 --> 00:12:35,504
Besides, I don't have time
to pretend I know all about it.

197
00:12:35,588 --> 00:12:36,881
But

198
00:12:36,964 --> 00:12:39,550
your attention to detail,

199
00:12:43,512 --> 00:12:45,556
All right, I'm listening.

200
00:12:47,892 --> 00:12:50,060
Things have been too quiet.

201
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:52,813
Nothing's happening. It's boring.

202
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:55,816
Which means I'm not getting any kickbacks.

203
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:57,401
That won't do.

204
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:58,444
What about my business?

205
00:12:58,527 --> 00:13:01,071
What about my plans for this country?

206
00:13:02,198 --> 00:13:03,365
So here's the plan.

207
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:17,296
Are you sure you still want
to stick with "Sinigang Cartel"?

208
00:13:17,796 --> 00:13:21,050
Don't you want to update it
to something cooler?

209
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:23,761
No. Sinigang stays.
It's got that sour kick.

210
00:13:26,263 --> 00:13:29,141
All right, fine.
That's what you're known for.

211
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:32,478
But if you're bringing back
the Sinigang Cartel,

212
00:13:32,561 --> 00:13:35,231
you'll need something
with an even stronger bite.

213
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:39,485
GAGO's achievements are no joke.

214
00:13:41,654 --> 00:13:43,405
You've got a point, Jake.

215
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:45,783
Of course, I never make half-baked plans.

216
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:49,286
There's still Chiara Valtrovi.

217
00:13:51,455 --> 00:13:54,708
She's still La Fornarina.

218
00:14:00,673 --> 00:14:04,260
And she's the one who defeated
La Morte Bianca.

219
00:14:04,343 --> 00:14:10,224
That's why she's a living legend,
an unbeatable one.

220
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:20,150
<i>So I'm assuming it's another</i>
<i>slow day at the agency?</i>

221
00:14:20,234 --> 00:14:21,610
<i>Nothing much going on?</i>

222
00:14:21,694 --> 00:14:23,529
Yes, not much happening.

223
00:14:23,612 --> 00:14:25,823
It's been pretty chill around the office.

224
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:31,370
You.

225
00:14:31,996 --> 00:14:33,205
<i>How are you doing?</i>

226
00:14:33,289 --> 00:14:35,374
Honestly. Tell me.

227
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:39,044
You know, this has been
a learning experience for me.

228
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:42,089
I feel like this is the first time

229
00:14:42,172 --> 00:14:44,967
I've been honest about how I really feel.

230
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:49,179
I'm used to staying on high alert
whenever we're on a mission.

231
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:51,807
I'm used to thinking
and acting tactically.

232
00:14:52,516 --> 00:14:54,268
And I'm also used

233
00:14:54,351 --> 00:14:57,187
to taking action first
before dealing with my feelings.

234
00:14:58,397 --> 00:15:00,190
<i>That turned out to be the side effect.</i>

235
00:15:00,691 --> 00:15:03,652
I overlooked how I should've
handled my emotions.

236
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:06,947
Especially

237
00:15:08,115 --> 00:15:10,409
the feelings I'd been hiding.

238
00:15:12,077 --> 00:15:14,288
The feelings I kept bottled up inside.

239
00:15:15,414 --> 00:15:16,415
<i>You know, Mikoy.</i>

240
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:19,335
<i>I was just being honest about how I felt.</i>

241
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:24,590
<i>But I wasn't expecting anything.</i>

242
00:15:24,673 --> 00:15:26,717
<i>Even if that's how I felt,</i>

243
00:15:27,509 --> 00:15:30,179
<i>I just hope we can still be friends.</i>

244
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:33,807
Thanks, Alex.

245
00:15:39,229 --> 00:15:42,524
It's really hard when you don't
process your emotions properly.

246
00:15:43,442 --> 00:15:45,694
<i>It feels so heavy.</i>

247
00:15:45,778 --> 00:15:48,030
Like you're carrying extra baggage.

248
00:15:48,906 --> 00:15:50,741
<i>You can say that again, Bok.</i>

249
00:15:50,824 --> 00:15:53,327
Just look at you. I know you so well.

250
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:56,163
<i>Your shoulders are always up</i>
<i>like you're on high alert.</i>

251
00:15:56,246 --> 00:15:57,706
Like this.

252
00:15:57,790 --> 00:16:01,543
You can never relax.
You're always so tense.

253
00:16:02,044 --> 00:16:03,921
You really do know me.

254
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:08,217
But you know, before I came here,

255
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:09,927
I was really nervous.

256
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:14,181
I thought it might be awkward.

257
00:16:15,474 --> 00:16:16,850
But all I did was

258
00:16:16,934 --> 00:16:21,063
take a deep breath
and be honest about my feelings.

259
00:16:21,146 --> 00:16:22,856
And honestly,

260
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,984
it made me feel so much lighter.

261
00:16:25,067 --> 00:16:27,569
Especially after seeing Mikoy and Chiara

262
00:16:28,153 --> 00:16:30,781
building a simple life here in Albay.

263
00:16:31,907 --> 00:16:33,492
You know, Bok,

264
00:16:33,575 --> 00:16:35,661
all I felt was genuine happiness for them.

265
00:16:40,457 --> 00:16:42,960
I get what you're saying.

266
00:16:43,043 --> 00:16:45,713
But didn't you also say

267
00:16:45,796 --> 00:16:48,340
that Chiara is very unpredictable?

268
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,885
Sometimes she's spontaneous.

269
00:16:51,969 --> 00:16:53,303
She has a mind of her own.

270
00:16:53,387 --> 00:16:55,264
She does things her own way.

271
00:16:55,764 --> 00:16:58,225
So how are you going to convince her
to go along with your plan?

272
00:16:59,309 --> 00:17:00,853
You're right again, Jake.

273
00:17:01,353 --> 00:17:04,148
But at the end of the day

274
00:17:04,231 --> 00:17:06,734
La Fornarina

275
00:17:06,817 --> 00:17:10,946
is a loving and devoted daughter.

276
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:13,782
She'll do anything for her parents,

277
00:17:13,866 --> 00:17:17,661
Viktor and Donabel.

278
00:17:24,793 --> 00:17:26,086
Exactly!

279
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:28,964
Just like the PBA's 50 Greatest Players!

280
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:32,885
I don't get it.

281
00:17:34,219 --> 00:17:35,763
Okay, let's just drop it.

282
00:17:41,977 --> 00:17:42,978
Sour!

283
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:44,688
That's what I like!

284
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:46,815
- Good, right?
- Yes, it's got that tang.

285
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:49,985
Wow, Bok.

286
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:53,363
You know, Bok, I'm so, so proud of you.

287
00:17:53,947 --> 00:17:56,408
I really am. I'm so proud of you. Why?

288
00:17:56,492 --> 00:17:58,494
You faced your insecurities
and your fears.

289
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:01,246
You went there to see them, okay?

290
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:03,499
You even faced your own feelings.

291
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:05,626
Honestly, right now,

292
00:18:09,296 --> 00:18:10,756
I really can't hide it.

293
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:13,467
You have no idea
how happy I am for you, Bok.

294
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:15,594
<i>I'm so proud of you.</i>
<i>And another thing, Bok.</i>

295
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:19,056
I don't think you'll have to force
yourself to be maid of honor anymore.

296
00:18:19,139 --> 00:18:21,475
<i>I remember the last time</i>
<i>we talked about that.</i>

297
00:18:21,558 --> 00:18:25,521
And now I think you and Chiara
have built a genuine connection.

298
00:18:25,604 --> 00:18:27,147
A real friendship.

299
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:30,275
Thanks to you too, Bok.

300
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:32,903
You've been so patient with me.

301
00:18:32,986 --> 00:18:35,614
And you never stopped reminding me.

302
00:18:36,323 --> 00:18:40,369
You never just checked whether I was safe.

303
00:18:40,452 --> 00:18:43,038
<i>You also checked how I was doing inside.</i>

304
00:18:43,122 --> 00:18:46,208
I'm really grateful to have
a friend like you.

305
00:18:46,291 --> 00:18:47,501
Thanks, Bok.

306
00:18:50,170 --> 00:18:53,465
That's what best buddies are for, right?

307
00:18:54,758 --> 00:18:58,053
Speaking of buddies,
how are Cocoy and Carlota?

308
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:01,723
Hey, wait. Remember
when we first joined the agency?

309
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:03,267
We were just like them.

310
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:05,435
Just like Cocoy and Carlota, right?

311
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:09,064
- Yes. Such show-offs!
- Such show-offs!

312
00:19:11,733 --> 00:19:13,902
We're still show-offs to this day.

313
00:19:13,986 --> 00:19:15,612
Well, that's true.

314
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:19,199
As for Carlota and Cocoy,
they're doing fine.

315
00:19:20,409 --> 00:19:22,828
They're not doing anything unusual.

316
00:19:22,911 --> 00:19:25,706
I've just noticed
they've been pretty busy lately.

317
00:19:26,623 --> 00:19:28,375
Busy? Working on what?

318
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:29,585
What's it about?

319
00:19:37,301 --> 00:19:40,053
We've brought the favor you asked for.

320
00:20:07,581 --> 00:20:11,126
Didn't you say it was
a slow day at the agency?

321
00:20:12,169 --> 00:20:13,503
<i>Hold on a second.</i>

322
00:20:13,587 --> 00:20:15,756
I know you're dating Carlota,

323
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:17,716
but you still need
to keep an eye on those two.

324
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:19,843
Bok, Bok.

325
00:20:19,927 --> 00:20:22,471
You know me. We're best buddies.
You should know this.

326
00:20:22,554 --> 00:20:24,431
I know we should keep

327
00:20:24,514 --> 00:20:27,726
our professional
and personal lives separate. Okay?

328
00:20:27,809 --> 00:20:30,312
And you know how I am
when it comes to work.

329
00:20:30,395 --> 00:20:32,189
I'm not just overly prepared.

330
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:33,482
I overreact too.

331
00:20:33,565 --> 00:20:36,944
But we're talking about
Cocoy and Carlota here.

332
00:20:37,027 --> 00:20:40,280
<i>They're highly skilled</i>
<i>and a huge asset to the agency.</i>

333
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:42,366
But we still have to watch them.

334
00:20:42,449 --> 00:20:45,369
We can't let our guard down
just because things are calm for now.

335
00:20:48,872 --> 00:20:51,792
They're not doing anything

336
00:20:52,709 --> 00:20:55,337
out of the ordinary.

337
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:57,256
Nothing suspicious at all.

338
00:20:57,839 --> 00:20:59,299
Okay? So you…

339
00:21:01,301 --> 00:21:02,302
Loosen up.

340
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:05,222
Your shoulders are getting
all tense again. Relax, Bok.

341
00:21:07,599 --> 00:21:08,767
All right.

342
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:10,727
See you.

343
00:21:17,859 --> 00:21:20,028
Alex! Alex!

344
00:21:20,112 --> 00:21:21,571
Alex.

345
00:21:21,655 --> 00:21:22,948
What is it?

346
00:21:23,448 --> 00:21:24,950
We've got a problem.

347
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:26,618
What problem?

348
00:21:26,702 --> 00:21:28,120
We've got a problem.

349
00:21:45,345 --> 00:21:48,557
I've missed this perfect pairing.

350
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:57,065
It's got the perfect balance
of heat and tang.

351
00:21:57,566 --> 00:22:01,069
As you already know,
here in the safehouse,

352
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:03,238
you can't be too picky.

353
00:22:07,951 --> 00:22:13,040
All they ever serve us here
is Pancit Canton,

354
00:22:13,123 --> 00:22:14,499
the…

355
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:17,878
original flavor.

356
00:22:21,590 --> 00:22:23,342
Original Pancit Canton.

357
00:22:40,734 --> 00:22:43,111
With the original flavor,

358
00:22:43,195 --> 00:22:44,738
you can get creative.

359
00:22:44,821 --> 00:22:48,241
You can elevate your instant meal

360
00:22:48,325 --> 00:22:50,869
with whatever protein
or vegetables you like.

361
00:22:52,370 --> 00:22:55,665
And you can adjust the flavor

362
00:22:55,749 --> 00:22:57,459
however you're feeling that day.

363
00:23:04,091 --> 00:23:05,634
Something like that.

364
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:31,576
What's the problem?

365
00:23:32,494 --> 00:23:34,621
It's Mikoy and Chiara.

366
00:23:34,704 --> 00:23:37,290
They're having trouble dancing together.

367
00:23:37,374 --> 00:23:39,584
Oh gosh, Chiara. Not like that.

368
00:23:39,668 --> 00:23:43,046
So you're saying Mikoy and Chiara
aren't dancing in sync?

369
00:23:43,130 --> 00:23:44,798
That seems impossible.

370
00:23:45,715 --> 00:23:47,843
See for yourself.

371
00:23:47,926 --> 00:23:50,053
See? They can't seem to stay in sync.

372
00:24:07,362 --> 00:24:08,363
Let's go, Mikoy!

373
00:24:09,364 --> 00:24:11,867
We can do just as well as Mom and Dad.

374
00:24:11,950 --> 00:24:13,118
We just have to trust each other.

375
00:24:13,201 --> 00:24:14,578
Absolutely.

376
00:24:14,661 --> 00:24:17,581
We've been through so much together.
This is just a dance floor.

377
00:24:17,664 --> 00:24:18,748
Exactly.

378
00:24:28,592 --> 00:24:29,426
I was wrong.

379
00:24:39,394 --> 00:24:41,438
<i>Well, you know what's frustrating?</i>

380
00:24:41,521 --> 00:24:43,315
You're talking to me just to judge me.

381
00:24:43,398 --> 00:24:45,692
But it turns out you already had
a fixed assumption,

382
00:24:45,775 --> 00:24:48,320
and now all you want
is for me to validate it.

383
00:24:48,403 --> 00:24:49,571
Right?

384
00:24:50,572 --> 00:24:52,365
Then go be with her!

385
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:58,121
Because isn't what really matters
that no matter what song life plays,

386
00:24:58,705 --> 00:25:00,081
we'll always dance through it together?

387
00:25:00,165 --> 00:25:02,167
Isn't that what truly matters?

388
00:25:11,259 --> 00:25:12,844
Come on, let's try again.
